{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Consumption.</b> His flesh wastes away and shrivels." "<b>Fever.</b> From the language of ״כִּי אֵשׁ קָדְחָה בְאַפִּי״ (Deuteronomy 32) — a fire of fevers; מלו״וי בְּלַעַז, which is very hot." "<b>Inflammation.</b> Hotter than קַדַּחַת, and they are all types of illnesses." "<b>Burning heat.</b> An illness that heats up inside the body, with constant thirst for water; and in לַעַז אישטרד״ימנט — from the language of ״וְעַצְמִי חָרָה מִנִּי חֹרֶב״ (Job 30), ״נָחַר מַפֻּחַ מֵאֵשׁ״ (Jeremiah 6)." "<b>And with the sword.</b> He will bring armies upon you." "<b>And with mildew and with blasting.</b> A plague of grain in the fields." "<b>Mildew.</b> An east wind; אשלי\"דה בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>Blasting.</b> Drying up — the face of the grain turns pale and becomes greenish; קמ\"א (variant — קרו\"א) בְּלַעַ\"ז." "<b>Until you perish.</b> Targum: ״עַד דְּתֵיבָד״ — that is, until you are destroyed — that they be consumed from you."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French malotie/maladie, 'disease'.", 3 "the la'az is Old French estredient, 'constraint/griping' (of a malady).", 6 "the la'az is Old French escaillide or similar, denoting a hot, scorching east wind.", 7 "the la'az is likely Old French cugnée or related; the variant reading קרו\"א is noted in the witnesses."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:41.041555039Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}